{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7K3GEGzqFBykUdYT7tr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, there's one thing I need to raise, plus a few questions.\n\n**The promise.** Your own setup gives each customer a regular cleaner *and a named backup*. So \"the same cleaner every single time\" isn't what you actually offer, and with 7 of 18 cleaners leaving last year, some customers will see a change again. These are people who left partly over this exact issue. If you break the promise a second time, they're unlikely to come back again. I'd suggest \"your own regular cleaner, plus one named backup you'll know by name, never a stranger.\" That's still a strong promise, and it's one you can keep.\n\nA few questions:\n\n1. **Can you go with the \"regular cleaner + named backup\" wording?** If you really can guarantee one person every time (for example, by skipping a visit rather than sending the backup), tell me how that works and I'll write it that way.\n2. **Does the $99 offer have a deadline or any conditions?** For example, does it need a recurring booking, or is it only for a 3-bedroom?\n3. **How should they rebook?** A link, a phone number, or just replying to the email?\n4. **Should I address price directly?** I could say you're $25 more than the apps because your cleaners are insured employees paid $21 an hour, or I could just lead with the $99 offer and leave price out.\n5. **Who signs it?** Your name and title, and the company name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_read_input_tokens":9533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":438},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"